  "notes": "A Descript-like audio editor for students: the transcript is the editing surface (strike-out cuts), and the timeline carries colour-coded waveform clips. Each source/speaker gets one colour (teal narration, olive sound, indigo Don Arturo, magenta Abuela Rosa), reused in the bin's left stripes, transcript speaker names, the clip-header square and the timeline clips. Teacher feedback works as time-anchored annotations: numbered amber markers on the ruler and in the transcript, plus side-panel cards with category tags (Pronunciation/Structure), Done checkboxes and status callouts that say whether the issue is still there, each with a corrective CTA (Re-record this line). The length meter is a segmented bar measured against a 4:00 target, with a red over-limit marker; the timeline ruler shows a red dashed 4:00 limit line and hatched overflow. The Rubric tab (seen live) shows a 75/100 score with per-criterion bars. Warm off-white neutrals, small radii (3–10px), mono timecodes. Bilingual Spanish content with English UI chrome."
}
